<title>GREECE: Greek Intrasoft wins 3.4bln drs EU deal.</title>
<headline>Greek Intrasoft wins 3.4bln drs EU deal.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-01-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greek informatics firm Intrasoft signed a four-year deal with an option for another year worth 3.4 billion drachmas, or 11.08 million ecus, with the informatics directorate of the EU commission, the company said in a statement.</p>
<p>The firm will maintain and support the LAN and WAN data networks of the EU commission in Brussels, Luxemburg and Strasbourg, it said.</p>
<p>Intrasoft beat out well-known companies such as Bull, Digital, Siemens, Telindus and Triple-P in winning the international tender, it said.</p>
<p>--Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
